Oversteer, https://github.com/berarma/oversteer
Commit 7f6b3ad8ebedb23b8d5c3d32e63ae653f4d02480, file data/udev/99-logitech-wheel-perms.rules,
unchanged. GPL-3.0: text in LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt in the SparkOS repository, installed as
/usr/share/licenses/sparkos-device-rules/oversteer/LICENSE.

The same file as in Universal Blue's oversteer-udev 0.0.git.415.7f6b3ad8 package on Bazzite. It
lets the signed-in user change a Logitech racing wheel's settings (rotation range, force feedback,
LEDs), for example from Oversteer on Flathub, without root. It matches only the wheels' product
IDs, so Logitech mice, keyboards and webcams are untouched.

Left out: the package's other two files. 99-thrustmaster-wheel-perms.rules and
99-fanatec-wheel-perms.rules only act on out-of-tree drivers (hid-tmff2, hid-t150,
hid-fanatecff) that Fedora's kernel doesn't have; the Fanatec one otherwise just makes every
Fanatec USB device writable by every user.
